{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"frowsy-beggarly-mammoth","creation_channel":"cli","description":"An unrelated change's Verified Gate run cancels an in-flight run for a different change, and Gerrit's CI bot turns that cancellation into a Verified -1. The change under review is then blocked on a vote that reflects no test result at all.\n\n## Observed\n\nChange 1615, patch set 2 (run 31560638673). Every one of the 14 completed jobs passed, including all four pytest matrix cells. The bounded mutation gate had been running 30m16s (03:39:25 -> 04:09:41) when it was cancelled, and the run's own conclusion is 'cancelled'. Gerrit's message reads:\n\n    Patch Set 2: Code-Review-1 Verified-1\n    CANCELLED: https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/31560638673\n\nThe cancellation timestamp 04:09:41 is the SAME SECOND that run 31562353593 was created. That run is a Gerrit Verified Gate run which Gerrit never associated with change 1615 (its messages only ever name 31560638673 for patch set 2), i.e. it belongs to a different change.\n\n## Why this is distinct from the two known causes\n\n- NOT the predates-the-gate mutation failure (sapphire-vulnerable-fruitfly): 1615 patch set 2 was already rebased onto current origin/main. The timings separate the two cleanly - patch set 1's mutation job died in 29s with scripts/mutation_gate.py absent (exit 2), while patch set 2's ran 30m16s of real work before cancellation.\n- NOT the s3_doctor bad-object transient (wrongful-chemic-squeaker): that did not recur on this run; the pytest cells were green.\n\n## Mechanism\n\nThe Verified Gate workflow's concurrency group appears not to include the change/patchset in its key, so a newly started run cancels an in-progress one. The bounded mutation gate makes a run take ~30 minutes, which is a wide window: any two changes under review within half an hour of each other can cancel one another.\n\n## Impact\n\nA -1 that carries no test signal. The only remedy today is recheck, which re-enters the same race - and under a busy queue a change can be starved indefinitely. It also burns a full 30-minute mutation run each time.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1: the Verified Gate workflow's concurrency group key includes the change (and patchset) so runs for different changes cannot cancel each other.\n- [ ] AC2: a run for the SAME change/patchset still supersedes its predecessor (re-pushing should not leave two runs racing to vote).\n- [ ] AC3: reproduce the current behavior first - two changes' Verified runs overlapping, one cancelled - then show it no longer occurs after the key change.\n- [ ] AC4: if a run is cancelled for any reason, the CI bot does not cast Verified -1, since a cancellation is not a test verdict (or it votes with a message that says so explicitly).","id":"be9d-2f2d-47ca-45d2","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Gerrit Verified Gate runs cancel each other: concurrency group is not keyed per-change"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786507948110083001,"uuid":"e3730c0b-3f8f-415b-91b8-b5a7d3dbe0ab"}